# Milestone: M3
# Covers: a host-registered finalizable type runs its destroy callback when
#         the last reference is dropped and the GC collects the cell.
#
# blocked: no finalizer->host-fn bridge for a script-creatable type
# matrix-row: gc-finalizer
#
# The `## host: expect-host-call <n>` directive exists and its generic
# host-callback-observation path is exercised by
# tests/chk/gc/expect_host_call.chk.  This fixture stays blocked on the OTHER
# prerequisite: there is no way for a host to register a finalizable type.
#   - The collector's finalize hook is uvm_gc_finalize (src/rt/uexec.c),
#     which switches on UCellType and frees the non-cell memory each
#     built-in kind owns.  It is per-KIND and internal -- there is no slot
#     in it for a host callback, and no host cell kind to attach one to.
#   - <urbi/urbi.h> exposes no type-registration entry point, so a fixture
#     cannot create the FileHandle of the original scenario nor route its
#     destroy through a counting host fn.
#
# No C-level coverage of a HOST finalizer, because there is nothing to
# cover.  The internal hook itself is exercised on every collection and
# asserted indirectly by tests/rt/test_leaks.c, which requires the
# allocator's live count back at zero after each suite.
#
# Activating this fixture needs a public finalizable-type registration API
# with a host destroy callback -- a v1.x API question, not a test-harness
# one.  The generic expect-host-call mechanism is proven separately in
# expect_host_call.chk.
